---
layout: base.njk
title: L'Archive / Forgotten Industries Taxonomy
description: The native Forgotten Industries filing authority for public layers, record families, evidence states, and lifecycle.
permalink: /archive/taxonomy/
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<section class="masthead">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <p class="section-label">L'Archive / {{ taxonomy.native.id }} / {{ taxonomy.native.status }}</p>
    <h1>Forgotten Industries Taxonomy</h1>
    <p class="tagline">
      Four controlled axes for filing the institution's own records: public
      layer, record family, evidence state, and lifecycle.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="evidence-band">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">Working Authority</p>
      <h2>Our language first.</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>{{ taxonomy.native.rule }}</p>
      <p>
        A record receives one public layer and one record family. Evidence state
        remains separate from lifecycle, physical condition, access, and longer
        operational notes. A missing assignment stays visibly unassigned; it is
        not inferred from tone or publication alone.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="source-band" id="public-layers">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">Axis 01 / {{ taxonomy.native.publicLayers.label }}</p>
      <h2>{{ taxonomy.native.publicLayers.question }}</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="link-list archive-record-list">
      {% for term in taxonomy.native.publicLayers.terms %}
      <li>
        <p class="entry-note">{{ term.id }} / {{ term.records.length | countLabel("indexed record", "indexed records") }}</p>
        <h3><a href="{{ term.url }}">{{ term.label }}</a></h3>
        <p>{{ term.definition }}</p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="evidence-band" id="record-families">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">Axis 02 / {{ taxonomy.native.recordTypes.label }}</p>
      <h2>{{ taxonomy.native.recordTypes.question }}</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="link-list archive-record-list">
      {% for term in taxonomy.native.recordTypes.terms %}
      <li>
        <p class="entry-note">{{ term.id }} / {{ term.records.length | countLabel("indexed record", "indexed records") }}</p>
        <h3>
          {% if term.records.length %}<a href="{{ term.url }}">{{ term.label }}</a>{% else %}{{ term.label }}{% endif %}
        </h3>
        <p>{{ term.definition }}</p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="source-band" id="evidence-states">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">Axis 03 / {{ taxonomy.native.evidenceStates.label }}</p>
      <h2>{{ taxonomy.native.evidenceStates.question }}</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="link-list archive-record-list">
      {% for term in taxonomy.native.evidenceStates.terms %}
      <li>
        <p class="entry-note">{{ term.id }}</p>
        <h3>{{ term.label }}</h3>
        <p>{{ term.definition }}</p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="evidence-band" id="lifecycle">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">Axis 04 / {{ taxonomy.native.lifecycleStates.label }}</p>
      <h2>{{ taxonomy.native.lifecycleStates.question }}</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="link-list archive-record-list">
      {% for term in taxonomy.native.lifecycleStates.terms %}
      <li>
        <p class="entry-note">{{ term.id }}</p>
        <h3>{{ term.label }}</h3>
        <p>{{ term.definition }}</p>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mirror-band" id="source-vocabulary">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">Discovery Indexes / {{ taxonomy.sourceTerms | count }} preserved terms</p>
      <h2>Source language remains reachable.</h2>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p>
        These indexes preserve useful words already present in records. They are
        discovery vocabulary, not the controlled FI authority, and they are not
        silently normalized or promoted into evidence.
      </p>
      <ul class="link-list archive-record-list">
        <li>
          <p class="entry-note">{{ taxonomy.categories | count }} terms</p>
          <h3><a href="/archive/categories/">Source categories</a></h3>
          <p>Object classes, record lanes, platforms, and inherited dossier labels.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="entry-note">{{ taxonomy.tags | count }} terms</p>
          <h3><a href="/archive/tags/">Source terms and tags</a></h3>
          <p>Dossier themes, field handles, inventory terms, and recovered social hashtags.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="entry-note">{{ taxonomy.systems | count }} terms</p>
          <h3><a href="/archive/systems/">System contexts</a></h3>
          <p>Named machines, dossiers, restoration contexts, and operating environments.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p class="entry-note">{{ taxonomy.status | count }} notes</p>
          <h3><a href="/archive/status/">Source state notes</a></h3>
          <p>Evidence-bearing operational prose retained until a separate lifecycle value is assigned.</p>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="source-band" id="migration-order">
  <div class="section-inner band-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="section-label">Convergence Order</p>
      <h2>Stabilize before crosswalk.</h2>
    </div>

    <ol class="link-list archive-record-list">
      {% for step in taxonomy.native.migrationOrder %}
      <li><p>{{ step }}</p></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
